{"name":"Skeleton","hex":"#ebdecc","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"skeleton","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The system that provides support to an organism, where in vertebrates it is internal and consists of bones and cartilage, and external in some other animals.","An anthropomorphic representation of a skeleton."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To reduce to a skeleton; to skin; to skeletonize.","To minimize."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skeleton"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skeleton","blocks":[{"text":"A skeleton is the structural frame that supports the body of most animals. There are several types of skeletons, including the exoskeleton, which is a rigid outer shell that holds up an organism's shape; the endoskeleton, a rigid internal frame to which the organs and soft tissues attach; and the hydroskeleton, a flexible internal structure supported by the hydrostatic pressure of body fluids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Horse_and_Man.jpg/330px-Horse_and_Man.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skeleton","wikidata":"Q7881"},{"title":"Skeleton (sport)","blocks":[{"text":"Skeleton is a winter sliding sport in which a person rides a small sled, known as a skeleton bobsled, down a frozen track while lying face down and head-first. The sport and the sled may have been named for the sled's resemblance to a ribcage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/D%C3%A9part_de_skeleton_Amy_Williams.jpg/330px-D%C3%A9part_de_skeleton_Amy_Williams.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skeleton_(sport)","wikidata":"Q186190"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Hym-myrmicinae.gif/330px-Hym-myrmicinae.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1